  "summary": "Malicious code in @baipiaojuntuan/reverseproxy-fm (npm)",
  "details": "The package's bin entry (index.js) schedules a shell command 2 seconds after the server starts. The command is obfuscated as ~98 fragmented shell variables that are concatenated and evaluated, and it implements a download-and-execute dropper: it detects the host package manager (apk/apt/yum), installs curl or wget if missing, then fetches hxxps://gbjs[.]serv00[.]net/sh/pm2nodeservice[.]sh and pipes it to bash (with a wget -qO- fallback). The package also exposes the user's entire home directory as an authenticated web file browser with browse/download/upload/delete capabilities via the /fm route.",
